## Native components

### FFmpeg 9.0.2 (`ffmpeg.exe`, `ffprobe.exe`, `av*.dll`, `sw*.dll`)

- Build: morph-ffmpeg `9.0.2-1`, a trimmed build made for Morph (only the codecs, formats and filters
  Morph uses), https://github.com/renangomide/morph-ffmpeg/releases/tag/v9.0.2-1. Build scripts based on
  BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds (MIT).
- License: **GPL-3.0** (built with `--enable-gpl --enable-version3`). Text: `licenses\ffmpeg\LICENSE.txt`.
- Source code: FFmpeg tag `n9.0.2`, https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/n9.0.2. The complete
  corresponding source (FFmpeg, every library below at the exact revision, build scripts) is
  `morph-ffmpeg-9.0.2-1-source.tar.xz` on the same release page.
- The build statically includes: x264 and x265 (GPL-2.0-or-later), SVT-AV1 (BSD-3-Clause-Clear +
  AOM patent license), libvpx (BSD-3-Clause + patent grant), dav1d (BSD-2-Clause), libvmaf
  (BSD-2-Clause-Patent), Opus, libvorbis and libogg (BSD-3-Clause), LAME (LGPL-2.0-or-later),
  libiconv (LGPL-2.1-or-later), zlib (Zlib), libvpl (MIT), the NVIDIA codec headers and AMF headers
  (MIT), and the mingw-w64 runtime and winpthreads (ZPL / MIT). Exact revisions and configure flags:
  `licenses\ffmpeg\BUILDINFO.txt`; license texts: `licenses\ffmpeg\licenses\`.

